<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <NeutralLanguage>en-US</NeutralLanguage>
    <PackageId>Cynicszm.FlatFiles</PackageId>
    <Authors>Cynicszm</Authors>
    <Description>Reads and writes CSV, fixed-length and other flat file formats with a focus on schema definition, configuration and speed. Supports mapping directly between files and classes. A fork of FlatFiles by Travis Parks, continued for .NET 10. The assembly and namespaces are unchanged, and through 7.6.0 every type and member name was too, so only the package reference differed; 8.0.0 renames a few of them, each named in the changelog.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Cynicszm/FlatFiles</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Cynicszm/FlatFiles.git</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>csv;comma;tab;separated;value;delimited;flat;file;fixed;width;fixed-width;length;fixed-length;parser;parsing;parse</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>A record read through a type mapper no longer copies the parsed values out of the reader, the reader fills one array of parsed values for the whole read rather than a new one for every record, and a type mapper now parses each value into the member that holds it rather than boxing it on the way. Define&lt;T&gt; has also lost its new() constraint: a type with no parameterless constructor is built by handing its constructor the parsed values, matched to its parameters by name, which maps a positional record, a type whose properties are get-only, and a type that validates what it is given. Measured on 10,000 records of 13 columns, a delimited read allocated 741 bytes a record and now allocates 613, a fixed-length read 1,157 and now 1,029, and the same reads through a type mapper 879 and 388, 1,295 and 732. No breaking changes.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <SignAssembly>true</SignAssembly>
    <AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>FlatFiles.snk</AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>
    <Version>8.6.0</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Ships with the package: IntelliSense text, and a symbol package whose Source Link points at the commit. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <!-- Pack fails if the public API loses or changes a member relative to the last release, so a breaking
         change has to be declared here by moving the baseline, not discovered by a consumer. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
    <PackageValidationBaselineVersion>8.6.0</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyVersion>8.6.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>8.6.0.0</FileVersion>
    <PackageLicenseFile>UNLICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Update="Properties\Resources.Designer.cs">
      <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
      <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
      <DependentUpon>Resources.resx</DependentUpon>
    </Compile>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Update="Properties\Resources.resx">
      <Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
      <LastGenOutput>Resources.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
    </EmbeddedResource>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\UNLICENSE.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The generator is built before this package is packed, but nothing in the library refers to it:
         it runs inside the compiler, not beside the library. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\FlatFiles.Generator\FlatFiles.Generator.csproj"
                      ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"
                      OutputItemType="Analyzer" />
    <None Include="..\FlatFiles.Generator\bin\$(Configuration)\netstandard2.0\FlatFiles.Generator.dll"
          Pack="true"
          PackagePath="analyzers/dotnet/cs"
          Visible="false" />
    <!-- Declares FlatFilesGenerateAccessors to the compiler, so the generator can be told to write nothing.
         build applies to a project that references this package; buildTransitive to one that gets it through
         another package. -->
    <None Include="build\Cynicszm.FlatFiles.props"
          Pack="true"
          PackagePath="build;buildTransitive" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
